 "summary": "The post-PR surface is minimal and canonical: no compatibility artifacts, no `private` general infrastructure (the sqrt and artanh-domain helpers are public in their mirrored Mathlib paths, the subject-free four-vector lemmas in `Lorentz.Vector`), no exposed bodies, and `rapidity` carries a complete characteristic API (def, direction-invariance, both junk-value forms, tanh characterisation in both directions, exp/log and transverse-mass forms) with correct, non-looping `@[simp]` choices. Note that the PR description advertises `minkowskiProduct_self_eq_zero_iff_of_spatialPart_eq_smul` and a `BasicExtensions` bound that are not in the code; the shipped module docstrings themselves are accurate.",
